@page "/rules"
@attribute [AllowAnonymous]

@* Ordningsreglerna (B70). Godkänns vid registreringen; rapporter och moderering hänvisar hit. *@

<PageTitle>Rules</PageTitle>

<article class="rules" style="max-width: 44rem">
    <h1 class="h3">Rules</h1>
    <p class="lead">Taleshaven is a place to tell stories together. These rules keep it a good place for everyone.</p>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">Be respectful</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Treat the other players and the GM with respect, also when you disagree. Talk about the story, not the person.</li>
        <li>No harassment, threats, bullying or personal attacks – in posts, out of character or anywhere else on the site.</li>
        <li>No hate: nothing that attacks or demeans people for their ethnicity, religion, gender, sexuality, disability or similar.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">Keep the story a shared one</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Dark themes can be part of a story, but agree on them with your table. Use <code>[spoiler]</code> for things others may want to skip.</li>
        <li>Don't play other players' characters without their consent.</li>
        <li>Follow the GM's decisions at the table. If you can't agree, talk out of character or leave the campaign.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">Nothing illegal, no spam</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>No illegal content, no sexual content involving minors, and no links to malware or scams.</li>
        <li>Don't share other people's personal information (names, addresses, photos) without their permission.</li>
        <li>No advertising or spam.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">How moderation works</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Use <strong>Report</strong> in a post's "…" menu if something breaks the rules. The report goes to the campaign's GM and to the site's moderators.</li>
        <li>The GM moderates their own table and can hide posts and remove players from the campaign.</li>
        <li>The site's moderators can hide posts anywhere and can warn, suspend (you can read but not post) or ban accounts.</li>
        <li>A hidden post stays in the thread as "This post was hidden by a moderator", and the author sees the reason.</li>
        <li>Illegal content is removed, and may be reported to the police.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">Your account and your data</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Under <a href="Account/Manage/PersonalData">Personal data</a> you can download everything you have written and delete your account.</li>
        <li>When you delete your account, your posts stay in the stories but are shown as written by "Deleted user". If a post contains personal information you want removed, ask a moderator.</li>
    </ul>
</article>
